WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.490
It's Labor Day and we're here, why are we
here?

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.210
We take federal holidays off.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.540
We're here because we're trading Labor Day
for an entire week off.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.769
Next week, we will be off all of next week.

00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:14.059
Much needed for the staff and then back with
you for the debates and through the election.

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:17.960
But good thing we're here today because one
of the biggest stories of the last couple

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.000
of months in terms of its possible impact
on the presidential election broke over the

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.259
weekend, which has now been quadruply corroborated,
despite Donald Trump claiming it is all fake.

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:37.040
This is a story in which the Atlantic broke
a story claiming that officials who were on

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:47.750
a trip with Trump to France say that Trump
called troops who died losers and suckers.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.649
And it is a hugely instructive story from
the perspective of the evolution of damage

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:57.100
control, because the initial story was just
in the Atlantic and it talked about Donald

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.480
Trump repeatedly disparaging the intelligence
of service members, saying keep wounded service

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.610
members out of military parades.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.710
It wouldn't look good.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.689
And it even goes on to say that I don't know
if you remember that incident in 2018 where

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:17.240
Donald Trump decided while in France not to
go and honor the troops at a cemetery near

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.930
Paris that it was because of rain.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.909
And these individuals who have come forward
said it had nothing to do with rain.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:27.090
Trump was worried his hair would look bad
if it got wet.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:33.159
And he didn't think it was important again
to honor those who were losers and suckers,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.130
quoting Trump as saying, why should I go to
that cemetery?

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.369
It's filled with losers.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:43.570
Trump also during that trip referred to a
conversation sorry, during a conversation

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:50.270
referred to more than eighteen hundred Marines
who lost their lives at Bella Wood as suckers

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.290
for getting killed.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.680
Now, Donald Trump came out and said it's all
fake.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.369
Trump administration officials came out and
said it's all lies.

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:01.200
Except then the Associated Press corroborated
it.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.140
Senior defense official with firsthand knowledge
of events and a senior U.S. Marine Corps officer

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.720
said to the Associated Press, the report in
the Atlantic is correct.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.270
White House continued to insist it's fake
and it's phony.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.810
And then CNN Tripoli corroborated it.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:25.060
Donald Trump referred to fallen U.S. service
members in crude and derogatory terms during

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.020
that trip in November of 2018 to France.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.690
And then they said it's all fake.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.890
And then Fox News quadruply corroborated it.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:34.890
Take a look at this.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.750
This is Fox News now.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:42.000
John, I've spoken with two senior U.S. officials
who are on the trip to France who confirmed

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.170
to me key details in the Atlantic article
and the quotes attributed to the president.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:51.310
My source, a former Trump administration official,
told me when the president spoke about the

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.610
Vietnam War, he said it was a stupid war.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.450
Anyone who went was a sucker.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.650
The president would say about American veterans.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.790
What's in it for them?

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.140
They don't make any money.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.610
The source said it was a character flaw of
the president.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:07.060
He could not understand why someone would
die for their country.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.330
Not worth it.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.730
Regarding the French trip to mark the end
of World War One, according to this former

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.800
official, the president was not in a good
mood.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.300
French President Macron had said something
that made him mad.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.920
He questioned why he had to go to two cemeteries.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.700
Why do I have to do two?

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:27.730
His staff explained he could cancel, but he
was warned they the press are going to kill

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.730
you for this.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:33.310
The president was mad as a hornet when they
did, according to this source, when asked

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:37.470
if the president could have driven to the
Ein Mahne cemetery.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:42.690
This former official said confidently that
there was not a security reason to not to

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.140
drive to the cemetery, which is about 40 miles
from Paris.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.550
Quote, The president drives a lot.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:51.590
The other world leaders drove to the cemeteries.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.950
He just didn't want to go.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:58.170
Regarding the president's July 4th military
parade planning during a planning session

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:04.000
at the White House after seeing the Bastille
Day parade in 2017, President Trump said regarding

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.650
the inclusion of wounded guys, quote, That's
not a good look.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.790
Americans don't like that.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:15.570
Regarding Senator McCain, the president, according
to this source, just hated John McCain.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.880
He always asked, why do you see him as a hero?

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.890
Two sources confirmed the president did not
want the flags lowered after McCain died.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.880
But others in the White House ordered them
at half mast.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.820
There was a standoff and then the president
relented.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:34.210
That is Fox News corroborating and expanding
the story.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:40.470
It's even worse than initially reported, actually,
based on Fox News's additional reporting.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.980
I'm starting to think this story may be true.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.950
And, of course, it tracks completely with
Donald Trump's brand.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:52.290
And a lot of this stuff he came close to saying
in public, including about John McCain, the

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:58.810
late Republican Senator John McCain, who had
been captured and held as a.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:04.830
Prisoner of war Donald Trump saying he prefers
soldiers who don't get captured and even tweeted

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.830
about it.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.080
I'll tell you about that in a moment.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.620
The internal chaos that this caused, that
Fox News, fascinating because you had at one

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:19.060
point within hours the opinion, people saying
this is all fake and the news side saying

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:23.890
we've been able to independently confirm these
reports.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:30.440
And Trump fundamentally is not able to understand
the concept of someone doing something that's

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.690
not completely self-centered and greedy.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.520
He has an inability to do that.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.431
And, you know, when this story broke, you
had some people on the left saying, Trump

00:05:38.431 --> 00:05:39.990
is right, these people are suckers.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.910
Who the hell would join the military?

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:47.950
I do think it's important to distinguish between
supporting the troops and supporting individual

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.080
wars and what the military does.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:58.370
I recognize, for example, that when George
W. Bush took us into the hairbrained, misguided

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:06.230
Iraq war, we didn't have a draft in which
I could have been drafted, potentially because

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.000
we have a volunteer army.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.380
And people actually volunteer.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.440
Now, we often send them to the wrong wars.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:19.250
We use the troops in disgusting ways for political
battles.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.770
The way George W. Bush did.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:28.950
But nevertheless, I don't think it makes sense
to denigrate the individuals as the suckers.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.530
We have a military industrial complex.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.860
That is the problem.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.110
We have a deranged foreign policy apparatus.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:44.810
And, you know, if if you do believe that those
who go and fight are suckers tone down the

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.500
military apparatus.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:47.610
Trump has done the opposite.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:53.310
Trump simultaneously brags about making the
military bigger than ever, but then says that

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:57.830
the individual troops are suckers and losers
when they actually go and get killed.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.050
And why is that?

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:05.100
It's because Trump doesn't care about the
individuals in the military.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:10.450
But Trump is glad to use the military as an
institution for his benefit when he can.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.030
It's very much on brand.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.810
In fact, could this be Trump's 47 percent
moment?

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.010
Thinking back to Mitt Romney in the 2012 campaign?

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:24.150
It's possible this you know, a lot of these
things that happen don't directly relate.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:28.669
They don't directly affect constituencies
that Trump needs.

00:07:28.669 --> 00:07:33.120
This is a case where if you look at Florida
and the heavy military presence in Florida

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.830
and Florida being an important battleground
state where it could determine it certainly

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.910
is much more likely than Massachusetts or
California to determine the winner of the

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:46.080
presidential election, disparaging the troops
in this way to the extent that people will

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.389
believe it could actually make a difference.

00:07:49.389 --> 00:07:53.450
And again, anybody doubting it, it's been
quadruply corroborated.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.630
It tracks with things Donald Trump has said
publicly.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:08:01.970
Remember John McCain, not a war hero because
he was captured attacking Goldstar family,

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.900
the Khan family.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:07.700
This is only half a step further than what
Trump has done publicly.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:12.380
And in fact, Donald Trump once did re tweet
that McCain is a loser.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:17.640
Trump retweeting in 2015 an article from Fitz
News, Donald Trump.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.300
John McCain is a loser.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.960
Now the stand the perspective.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.980
There was the election of 2008.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:29.050
But Trump very critical of McCain, including
for having been captured.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:34.460
And by the way, this is maybe the most interesting
thing Pete Buda judge has done.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:40.719
He was interviewed on Fox News about this
story and he used Fox News's own confirmation

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:43.980
of the story while on Fox News against them.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:44.980
Take a look at this again.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.990
I'm looking at the Internet right now.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:52.190
Fox News itself has confirmed many of the
details of this story.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:55.150
So so the real question is not to me.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.570
Did Trump do this?

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.310
It seems almost certain that he did.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:03.170
The question is, number one, what else is
going to come out between now and November?

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:06.050
Because the Atlantic is saying there will
be much more, that this is only the tip of

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.050
the iceberg.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:13.640
And number two, will this affect Trump with
constituencies he needs, like the military?

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.550
I believe that it could.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.930
I want to hear from you.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:18.830
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:47.220
Let me know what you think could be the impact

00:09:47.220 --> 00:10:05.080
of

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:33.110
this story.

